      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART X, LINE 2:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TCEI WAS FORMED AS A CALIFORNIA NONPROFIT CORPORATION AND IS CLASSIFIED BY THE IRS AS A 501(C)(3) PUBLICLY SUPPORTED ORGANIZATION, WHICH MEANS THAT IT IS GENERALLY EXEMPT FROM BOTH FEDERAL AND STATE INCOME TAXES. INCOME, IF ANY, THAT IS DEEMED TO BE UNRELATED BUSINESS TAXABLE INCOME ("UBTI") IS SUBJECT TO FEDERAL AND STATE INCOME TAXES. UBTI IS OPERATIONAL INCOME THAT IS NOT RELATED TO THE TAX-EXEMPT PURPOSE OF THE ORGANIZATION. DIVIDENDS, INTEREST, CERTAIN OTHER INVESTMENT INCOME, ROYALTIES, CERTAIN RENTAL INCOME, CERTAIN INCOME FROM RESEARCH ACTIVITIES AND GAINS OR LOSSES FROM THE DISPOSITION OF PROPERTY ARE EXCLUDED WHEN COMPUTING UBTI. DONORS MAY DEDUCT CHARITABLE CONTRIBUTIONS TO TCEI UNDER THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE SECTION 170(B)(1)(A)(VI). FOR UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS THAT MEET A "MORE LIKELY THAN NOT" THRESHOLD, TCEI RECOGNIZES THE BENEFIT OF UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS IN ITS FINANCIAL STATEMENTS. DURING THE YEAR ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2024 AND 2023, TCEI HAD NO UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS. TCEI RECORDS INTEREST AND PENALTIES, IF ANY, RELATED TO UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS AS A COMPONENT OF INCOME TAX EXPENSE. DURING THE YEAR ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2024 AND 2023, TCEI DID NOT RECOGNIZE A PROVISON FOR INCOME TAXES.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
